📄 Privacy Policy
Last Updated: 12 September 2026

1. Introduction  
This Privacy Policy explains how the HomeDev / HomeHermes Discord application (“the App”) collects, uses, and stores information.

2. Information We Collect  
The App only collects the minimum data required for functionality, including:

Discord user ID

Discord username

Messages sent to the bot (commands, interactions)

Server and channel IDs

Integration metadata (e.g., Telegram user ID if you connect your bot)

The App does not collect:

Email addresses

Phone numbers

Payment information

Sensitive personal data

3. How We Use Your Data  
Data is used solely to:

Process bot commands

Provide requested features

Maintain bot functionality

Improve reliability and performance

We do not sell, share, or monetize user data.

4. Data Storage & Security  
Data may be temporarily stored in logs or cache for debugging or operational purposes.
Reasonable technical measures are used to protect stored data.

5. Third‑Party Services  
If you connect external services (e.g., Telegram, Hermes Agent), those services may receive identifiers necessary for integration. Their privacy policies apply separately.

6. Data Retention  
Data is retained only as long as necessary for bot functionality. Logs may be periodically purged.

7. Children’s Privacy  
The App follows Discord’s minimum age requirements (13+ or regional equivalent).
We do not knowingly collect data from children under this age.

8. Your Rights  
You may request removal of stored data by contacting the developer.
You may also remove the bot from your server at any time.

9. Updates to This Policy  
This Privacy Policy may be updated. Continued use of the App indicates acceptance of the updated policy.

10. Contact  
For privacy questions, contact the developer via GitHub:
